// Title: Potentially Suspicious Rundll32.EXE Execution of UDL File
// Sigma ID: 0ea52357-cd59-4340-9981-c46c7e900428
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: @kostastsale
// Date: 2024-08-16 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, command-and-control, stealth, T1218.011, T1071
// Description: Detects the execution of rundll32.exe with the oledb32.dll library to open a UDL file. Threat
//   actors can abuse this technique as a phishing vector to capture authentication credentials or
//   other sensitive data.
// False positives:
//   - UDL files serve as a convenient and flexible tool for managing and testing database connections in various development and administrative scenarios.
// References:
//   - https://trustedsec.com/blog/oops-i-udld-it-again
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_udl_exec.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\explorer.exe" and (FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "RUNDLL32.EXE") and ((ProcessCommandLine contains "oledb32.dll" and ProcessCommandLine contains ",OpenDSLFile " and (ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Users\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Downloads\\")) and ProcessCommandLine endswith ".udl")
